# FullShot — .gitignore
#
# This repository has never existed before. The first `git add` is therefore
# the only one that has ever mattered: everything this file fails to exclude
# becomes permanent history the moment it is pushed, and a token that reaches a
# remote is compromised whether or not the commit is later removed.
#
# Written to be read, not just obeyed. Each block says WHY.
# Companion: GIT-SETUP.md at the repo root — it contains the verification
# commands that PROVE this file is doing its job. Do not skip them; a
# .gitignore is a claim, and an unverified claim is how this project's worst
# bugs have always started.


################################################################################
# 1. SECRETS  —  the highest-stakes lines in this file
################################################################################
# `.claude/secrets.env` holds a LIVE token and it lives inside the working
# tree. Nothing else stands between it and a public remote.
#
# Deliberately over-specified: the directory, the exact path, the basename
# anywhere in the tree, and the general shapes a future secret is likely to
# take. Four independent rules, so no single careless edit can uncover it.
#
# *** DO NOT ADD A `!` NEGATION ANYWHERE BELOW THAT COULD RE-INCLUDE THESE. ***
# In .gitignore the LAST matching rule wins, so a later un-ignore silently
# defeats an earlier ignore. See GIT-SETUP.md §5 before relaxing anything here.

.claude/
.claude/secrets.env
**/secrets.env
*.env
*.env.*
!*.env.example

# Other credential shapes — none exist in the tree today; these are here so
# that the day one appears, it is already excluded rather than newly at risk.
secrets/
credentials.json
.npmrc
# 🔴 ADDED 2026-08-20. `templates/tool/.gitignore` has carried these two lines
# since the skeleton was written; this file — the one that actually governs the
# only real tool — never did. Measured that day: `git check-ignore
# publish/upload-token.txt` came back NOT IGNORED here, and NOT IGNORED against
# HEAD too, so it is a gap this file has always had rather than one the zip fix
# below introduced. A store upload token is exactly the credential shape that
# would land in publish/ while somebody is wiring up a submission, and it is
# the directory whose zips are now deliberately tracked — so it is the last
# place that should be relying on nobody making a mistake.
publish/*.credentials
publish/upload-token*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*

# NOTE on *.pem: this also covers the Chrome Web Store item signing key that
# `chrome://extensions` → "Pack extension" drops next to the .crx. Losing that
# key means you can never update the published item; leaking it means someone
# else can sign as you. It belongs in a password manager, not in git.


################################################################################
# 2. DEPENDENCIES
################################################################################
# The only node_modules in the tree is test/e2e/node_modules (Playwright +
# a downloaded Chromium — hundreds of MB of platform-specific binaries).
# Reproduced by: cd test/e2e && npm ci && npx playwright install chromium
node_modules/


################################################################################
# 3. BUILD OUTPUTS  —  the store packages
################################################################################
# 🔴 THIS BLOCK USED TO IGNORE `publish/*.zip` AND THAT SILENTLY TURNED OFF A
# REAL CHECK. Corrected 2026-08-20, with the evidence below, because it
# contradicted BOTH of the other .gitignore files in this repository and the
# nested one wins for files beneath it — so the other two stated an intent that
# had never once taken effect here.
#
# What it used to say, kept because the reasoning is the part worth reading:
#
#     "publish/*.zip are build artifacts, not sources. They are regenerated by
#      node publish/package.node.js and are byte-derivable from the tracked
#      tree, so tracking them would only add ~1 MB of binary churn per release
#      and invite the classic mismatch where the committed zip is a version
#      behind the committed source."
#
# Both halves are wrong in the way that matters.
#
# "BYTE-DERIVABLE FROM THE TRACKED TREE" — from WHICH tracked tree? This
# repository has ZERO tags and ZERO releases, so there is no commit a past
# artifact can be re-derived from. And the comparison the packer wants is not
# against a rebuild; it is against the artifact a store actually received.
#
# "ONLY BINARY CHURN" — measured 2026-08-20: `node scripts/pack.mjs fullshot
# --target firefox` printed, in its own words,
#
#     "no previous release package for firefox in Extension/Full_Screen_Shot/
#      publish/ — the dropped-file floor graded 0 entries. That is correct for
#      a first package, and it is NOT a clean diff: nothing was compared. Keep
#      each released zip in publish/ (git tracks them deliberately) and the
#      next build is measured against it."
#
# That floor is scripts/pack.mjs's third: every entry of the last released
# package must be present in this build, which is how a silently dropped file
# is caught. It has graded ZERO for the only real tool in this repo, for the
# whole life of the repo, because of the one line below. templates/tool/
# .gitignore predicted it exactly: "know that you have turned the dropped-file
# check off, because it has nothing left to compare with."
#
# The version-drift worry was the one good point, and it is now held by tooling
# rather than by refusing to keep the file: scripts/pack.mjs compares against
# the most recent previous package and warns at an UNCHANGED version, and
# scripts/check-store-packages.mjs WARNs on any package whose version is not the
# tree's. A stale zip is now loud instead of absent.
#
# So: zips stay ignored everywhere in this tool EXCEPT publish/, which is the
# one place they are evidence rather than scratch. `publish/**` and `**/*.zip`
# are both in tool.json's package.exclude, so a tracked zip can never ride
# along inside a package.
#
# ⚠️ THE NEGATION BELOW IS NARROW ON PURPOSE. It re-includes exactly
# `publish/*.zip` and nothing else. It cannot reach the secrets in section 1:
# those are matched by separate patterns (.claude/, *.env, *.pem, *.key …), and
# a `!` only re-includes what its own pattern matches. Verified with
# `git check-ignore -v` on .claude/secrets.env, publish/upload-token and a
# stray root zip immediately after this edit.
*.zip
!publish/*.zip
*.crx
*.xpi
web-ext-artifacts/


################################################################################
# 4. TEST RENDER ARTIFACTS
################################################################################
# Both directories are WRITE-ONLY evidence: the sims and the Playwright run
# render PNGs there for a human to eyeball. Nothing reads them back as a
# golden, so a fresh clone that has never run the tiers is not missing an
# input — it is only missing last run's pictures, which `node test/...`
# regenerates. (Verified: no tier opens a file under either out/ directory.)
# If you later add true golden images, move them OUT of out/ and track them.
test/e2e/out/
test/pixel-sim/out/


################################################################################
# 5. Reference/
################################################################################
# Excluded for a licensing reason, not a size one: Reference/ holds UI
# screenshots used for comparison during development, including
# "GoFullPage_Full Page.png" — a capture of a competing commercial product.
# Redistributing someone else's product UI from a public repo is a copyright
# question nobody needs. It is also already excluded from the store package by
# publish/package.node.js's allowlist, so nothing ships from here either way.
Reference/


################################################################################
# 6. OS AND EDITOR DROPPINGS
################################################################################
# Windows
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk

# macOS
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
# NOT included: the usual macOS `Icon?` rule. On Windows and macOS git sets
# core.ignorecase=true and folds case when matching .gitignore, so `Icon?`
# ("Icon" + exactly one character) also matches the directory `icons` — and
# would silently drop all four shipped extension icons from the repository.
# The boilerplate rule is a real hazard in THIS tree; leaving it out is the fix.

# Linux
*~
.directory
.fuse_hidden*
.nfs*

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project


################################################################################
# 7. SCRATCH AND LOGS
################################################################################
# `shipprobe-DELETE-ME.txt` (0 bytes, repo root) is scratch left over from a
# packaging probe. It is matched below, but the right fix is to DELETE it
# rather than hide it — see COMPLIANCE-CHECKLIST.md E4 and GIT-SETUP.md step 1.
*DELETE-ME*
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
*.log
